ic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}(2n-1)^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.At $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is \n{{field-2}}\nat $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}={{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite our Fourier series as\n\n$$\nf(x)∼1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}x).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that at $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)=1.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is $\\text{continuous}$ at $x=0,$ the corresponding Fourier series converges to \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{(2n-1)\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0) \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}}\\cdot 1 \\\\ -1 & =-\\frac{8}{{\\pi }^{2}}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} \\\\ {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{(2n-1)^{2}} & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
